<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Nop.Tests - shared test infrastructure, migrated by task 4.5
    (Requirements 5.6, 5.3, 1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 3.1).

    This project is not a test suite for a particular library; it is the helper
    assembly that every other test project under src/Tests references
    (Nop.Core.Tests, Nop.Data.Tests, Nop.Services.Tests, Nop.Web.MVC.Tests). It
    holds TestsBase, the ShouldXxx assertion extensions, TypeAssert,
    ExceptionAssert and AttributeExtensions. It does, however, contain one real
    fixture of its own - ExceptionAssertTests, 4 tests - so it is wired as a
    runnable test project rather than a plain class library (see the test-SDK
    ItemGroup below).

    Converted from the classic (non-SDK) MSBuild format. Dropped in the conversion:
      * ToolsVersion / DefaultTargets / xmlns MSBuild 2003 attributes
      * ProjectGuid {1D9EB579-3630-468A-BE94-49E7DF4F6E1D}, ProductVersion,
        SchemaVersion, FileAlignment, AppDesignerFolder, TargetFrameworkProfile,
        OutputType (Library is the SDK default and is kept - see the note on
        OutputType further down), RootNamespace/AssemblyName (both already equal
        the project name, which is the SDK default)
      * TargetFrameworkVersion v4.5.1
      * The Debug|AnyCPU / Release|AnyCPU PropertyGroup pair, including
        Prefer32Bit and WarningLevel (the SDK supplies equivalent defaults)
      * Import of $(MSBuildToolsPath)\Microsoft.CSharp.targets and the commented
        BeforeBuild/AfterBuild target stubs
      * The explicit <Compile Include="..."/> list of 6 files - replaced by the
        SDK's implicit globbing
      * BCL <Reference Include="System.*"/> entries (System, System.Core,
        System.Data, System.Xml, System.Xml.Linq, System.Data.DataSetExtensions,
        Microsoft.CSharp) - subsumed by the net10.0 shared framework
      * The two <Reference/> items with HintPaths into ..\..\packages\ -
        nunit.framework and Rhino.Mocks - re-expressed below (NUnit) or dropped
        entirely (Rhino Mocks; see the RHINO MOCKS note)
      * <None Include="packages.config"/> - the file is deleted by this task
        (Requirements 1.3, 1.5)

    There was no app.config to migrate (Requirement 1.4 is vacuous here) and no
    System.Web usage at all in this project - see the FAKES note below.

    Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs is retained, matching Nop.Core / Nop.Data /
    Nop.Services; GenerateAssemblyInfo=false in src/Directory.Build.props keeps
    the SDK from emitting a duplicate set of assembly attributes.

    TargetFramework, Nullable, ImplicitUsings, GenerateAssemblyInfo and the shared
    assembly metadata come from src/Directory.Build.props; net10.0 is restated
    here so the target framework is verifiable from the project file itself
    (Requirement 1.2).
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>

    <!--
      OutputType is deliberately left at the SDK default (Library). Adding
      Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk does NOT force Exe - it only sets TestProject /
      IsTestProject - and VSTest runs the test assembly through its own testhost,
      so a library builds and runs tests fine. Keeping it a library also keeps
      this project a normal ProjectReference target for the four downstream test
      projects. Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk still injects an unused internal
      AutoGeneratedProgram.Main; it is internal, so it cannot collide with the
      one generated in each downstream test project.
    -->
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    packages.config -> PackageReference (Requirements 1.3, 1.5).

    Versions are governed centrally by src/Directory.Packages.props
    (ManagePackageVersionsCentrally=true, CentralPackageVersionOverrideEnabled=false),
    so every item below is intentionally version-less.

      NUnit                  advanced 3.6.1 -> 3.14.0. Used by ExceptionAssert.cs,
                             TypeAssert.cs and TestExtensions.cs (Assert,
                             TestFixture, Test, SetUp, TearDown, TestDelegate,
                             AssertionException).
      Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk NEW. Not in the legacy packages.config - under
                             .NET Framework these projects were run by an external
                             nunit3-console / the VS NUnit adapter installed
                             per-solution. On net10.0 the test host is a package,
                             so `dotnet test` needs it.
      NUnit3TestAdapter      NEW, same reason: the VSTest adapter that discovers and
                             executes NUnit fixtures under `dotnet test`.

    Both of the new entries exist specifically so this project is RUNNABLE and not
    merely compilable - that is the stated reason task 4.5 was promoted from
    optional to required (see the amended Notes section of tasks.md).

    RHINO MOCKS - DROPPED, NOT SUBSTITUTED.
    The legacy packages.config pinned RhinoMocks 3.6.1. Rhino Mocks was abandoned
    around 2012, its last release (3.6.1 / 4.0.0-alpha) is .NET Framework-only, and
    there is no net10.0-compatible version - so it cannot come along.

    It is dropped rather than replaced because, in THIS project, its entire usage
    was dead code:
      * TestsBase.cs held `protected MockRepository mocks;`, assigned
        `new MockRepository()` in [SetUp] and calling `mocks.ReplayAll()` /
        `mocks.VerifyAll()` in [TearDown]. Nothing anywhere in the repository ever
        created a mock through that instance. The five Nop.Services.Tests fixtures
        that do mock use the STATIC factory `MockRepository.GenerateMock<T>()`,
        which does not register with any MockRepository instance, so ReplayAll()/
        VerifyAll() always ran against an empty repository - i.e. they were no-ops
        and removing them changes no test outcome.
      * TestExtensions.cs had `using Rhino.Mocks.Constraints;` and referenced no
        type from it.
    No mocking framework is therefore declared here: this project has no mocking
    usage left, and declaring an unused package would break the direct-dependency
    rule the rest of this migration follows.

    NOT IN SCOPE OF THIS TASK, BUT FLAGGED: the downstream test projects DO use
    Rhino Mocks for real - `MockRepository.GenerateMock<T>()`, `.Expect(x => ...)`,
    `.Return(...)`, `Arg<T>.Is.Anything` - in Nop.Core.Tests, Nop.Services.Tests
    (5 fixtures) and Nop.Web.MVC.Tests. Those projects need a replacement chosen
    in their own tasks (2.6, 4.4, 17.1); NSubstitute is the closest in spirit
    (Substitute.For<T>(), .Returns(...), Arg.Any<T>(), .Received()). No such
    package is pinned yet - that decision is left to the user.

    FAKES: the task description anticipated System.Web-based fakes in this project.
    There are none - no file under src/Tests/Nop.Tests references System.Web at
    all, and there is no Fakes folder here. The Fake* seams live in Nop.Core
    (Nop.Core.Fakes.FakeHttpContext, re-implemented over a composed
    DefaultHttpContext because DefaultHttpContext is sealed in .NET 10, plus the
    new FakeSession : ISession, FakeIdentity and FakePrincipal) and are consumed
    directly by Nop.Core.Tests / Nop.Web.MVC.Tests, not through this project. So
    there was nothing to port and nothing to duplicate.

    No FrameworkReference is declared: nothing here binds to an ASP.NET Core type,
    and Nop.Core's own FrameworkReference to Microsoft.AspNetCore.App flows
    transitively through the ProjectReference below in any case.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" />
    <PackageReference Include="NUnit" />
    <PackageReference Include="NUnit3TestAdapter" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    ProjectReference to the already-migrated SDK-style Nop.Core (Requirement 2.4).
    Used by TestExtensions.PropertiesShouldEqual, which tests values against
    Nop.Core.BaseEntity. The legacy
    <Project>{6BDA8332-939F-45B7-A25E-7A797260AE59}</Project> / <Name>Nop.Core</Name>
    metadata children are dropped - the SDK resolves references by path.

    No signature churn from the Nop.Core / Nop.Data / Nop.Services migrations
    reaches this project: BaseEntity is unchanged, and this project touches none
    of the changed seams (WebHelper, PerRequestCacheManager, MemoryCacheManager,
    IDbContext.Set<T>, NopObjectContext, RouteValueDictionary, SelectList).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Core\Nop.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
